Yes, they're at least as good as regular longswords
and *slightly* better in some relatively minor way.

Vorpal Blade is slightly better because it has a
chance of instakill, but this isn't something that
can be relied upon at all, so its usefulness is quite
marginal.  Demonbane is slightly better because
it kills demons twice as fast, but demons are only
a minority of the things you face, even in Gehennom,
and with a couple of special exceptions they're
mostly not particularly dangerous (for a character
who gets that far into the game) in my experience.

If there were a Lichbane, that would be significantly
more useful than Demonbane (unless you have
blessed-genocided L, which, granted, is a popular
tactic and one I like to employ myself).  If Giantslayer
considered titans to be giants, it would arguably be
at least as good as Demonbane, even though titans
are rather rare.

Sunsword is better than a regular sword mainly
because it's also a light source.  (Undead, like
demons, are seldom a major threat.)  Granted,
it's a light source that doesn't run out of oil,
which is rather nice.

> > the longsword is one of the best non-artifact weapons
> > in the game;
>
> And the artifact longswords have the good basic property
> of the longswords plus their specific bonus.

Yes, granted.

I'd rather have any longsword (that doesn't destroy
monster inventory) than most other weapons in the
game.

But the weapons I really want, if my character can
wield them, are the ones that do double (or nearly
double) damage against all or nearly all monsters
in the game, without major averse effects.
Excalibur, Snickersnee, Grayswandir.
(This is a major advantage of being lawful.
OTOH, neutral characters get much better
non-weapon artifacts, not least the Eye.  I
haven't played enough chaotic characters to
really be clear on their advantages yet.)

I'd add Cleaver to that list if only it weren't two-handed.
Ditto the Staff of Whatshisname and the Tsuguri
of Whosit.  I don't think I'd call these junk as such,
but a two-handed weapon has some real caveats,
so they definitely aren't my first choice.  When I
had Cleaver as a Barbarian, I ended up using the
Sunsword that a random A in the Mines dropped
instead, even though it does less damage.)


